- The `memset(deltas,...)` calls are the kind of thing that can show up as a “WRITE of size 4” at the exact end (optimized memset often writes word-sized chunks).
- Clamping `clipx0/clipx1` prevents `skipx+clipn` from exceeding the allocated width-derived buffers.
- Clamping in `add_span_aa` prevents out-of-range edge x values from generating out-of-range indices even when other invariants are broken by crafted PDFs.

